    {
      "id": "claim_8047c18e21084514b7297710df19bf29",
      "statement": "Before a smoke run, `tools/hx-doc/hx-proof --ready <id>` gates whether a step may run: it reports READY only when every required prior step is PASS and the step itself is not NOT_EXECUTABLE or already PASS; NOT READY lists the blocking steps; a NOT_EXECUTABLE step reports NOT RUNNABLE because an implementation decision is still open. `hx-smoke-promote` enforces the same DAG at promotion, so there is no bypass flag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/03-runbooks/RUN-SHEET.md#L34-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8017cd631c13e5b8cb21bf7ed407d7f9a0a1ee500306581c2bc16732cbf5b2af:"
